WEBVTT

00:01:49.304 --> 00:01:55.076
This is footage from an unmanned
drone flying above the capital.

00:01:55.076 --> 00:01:58.213
While you can discern the intensity
of the anti-aircraft fire,

00:01:58.213 --> 00:02:01.549
it does not rely on radar or any
other guidance system,

00:02:01.549 --> 00:02:04.018
and produces little result.

00:02:04.018 --> 00:02:05.952
What are the losses for the
multinational forces?

00:02:07.255 --> 00:02:09.724
Virtually zero.

00:02:09.724 --> 00:02:12.760
Is Belgistan without radar?

00:02:12.760 --> 00:02:17.398
Tornado ECR's and A-12's, equipped
with anti-radar missiles,

00:02:17.398 --> 00:02:19.667
are on patrol at all times.

00:02:19.667 --> 00:02:22.470
We have reports telling us
that most radar facilities

00:02:22.470 --> 00:02:25.640
have switched off their systems
in fear of attack.

00:02:25.640 --> 00:02:31.012
But Colonel Stilbanov seems to be
maintaining an aggressive stance.

00:02:31.012 --> 00:02:32.680
Regarding that issue,

00:02:32.680 --> 00:02:37.452
preparations are proceeding for
stage three of our operations.

00:02:37.452 --> 00:02:39.554
Stage three?

00:02:39.554 --> 00:02:44.692
If Belgistan insists on ignoring the
demands made by the United Nations,

00:02:44.692 --> 00:02:47.862
we may have to deploy regular
forces in this engagement.

00:02:47.862 --> 00:02:51.432
But I've been informed there have been
disagreements within the UN

00:02:51.432 --> 00:02:56.638
regarding interpreting the causes
for the recent ground war losses.

00:02:56.638 --> 00:02:58.806
On that issue, I have no comment.

00:02:58.806 --> 00:03:02.410
Isn't the real reason for
the Security Council

00:03:02.410 --> 00:03:08.716
rushing preparations for a ground
campaign is to establish precedence

00:03:08.716 --> 00:03:11.185
before the neighboring nations can
attempt to negotiate a settlement?

00:03:11.185 --> 00:03:12.420
No comment.

00:03:12.420 --> 00:03:15.189
This will end today's briefing.

00:03:15.189 --> 00:03:19.294
How do you expect the neighboring
nations to accept actions such as this?

00:03:19.294 --> 00:03:21.319
Please wait, General Krause!

00:03:24.532 --> 00:03:28.536
Unit Two vertical stresses
plus minus 2.7 G.

00:03:28.536 --> 00:03:30.305
Horizontal stresses 1.8G.

00:03:30.305 --> 00:03:31.706
Blood pressure 180.

00:03:31.706 --> 00:03:34.442
Heart rate increased to 197.

00:03:34.442 --> 00:03:37.312
Unit Three, output 830 kilowatts.

00:03:37.312 --> 00:03:40.148
Section A of the right leg has sustained
twenty points of stress damage.

00:03:40.148 --> 00:03:41.849
Minus 4.3G.

00:03:41.849 --> 00:03:43.451
Blood pressure 195.

00:03:43.451 --> 00:03:45.253
Heart rate 211.

00:03:45.253 --> 00:03:47.551
Left transmission system,
crack detected in core!

00:03:55.563 --> 00:03:56.731
Time to stop.

00:03:56.731 --> 00:03:58.733
Captain Ataka, standby at
your current position.

00:03:58.733 --> 00:04:01.669
Once the recovery vehicle arrives, we
will ascertain the damage sustained.

00:04:01.669 --> 00:04:04.137
All remaining units, return to hangar
under your own power.

00:04:15.550 --> 00:04:18.686
So, will we be dispatched?

00:04:18.686 --> 00:04:21.389
No, it hasn't been finalized yet.

00:04:21.389 --> 00:04:25.626
I understand the overall position is
moving toward allowing deployment,

00:04:25.626 --> 00:04:29.364
but there is some tough resistance
to it within the cabinet.

00:04:29.364 --> 00:04:31.632
The constitution issue.

00:04:31.632 --> 00:04:34.035
It won't be easy getting around that.

00:04:34.035 --> 00:04:38.940
But I've heard Lieutenant Colonel
Hirokawa is on it.

00:04:38.940 --> 00:04:40.241
Knowing him,

00:04:40.241 --> 00:04:43.911
I won't be surprised if he forces
through the overseas deployment.

00:04:43.911 --> 00:04:49.650
Without waiting for the Security
Council's resolution,

00:04:49.650 --> 00:04:53.788
America mobilized their RDF.

00:04:53.788 --> 00:04:57.291
They clearly arbitrarily proceeded
with an unilateral decision.

00:04:57.291 --> 00:05:03.931
Even if we take this opportunity to
dispatch the TA's on our own,

00:05:03.931 --> 00:05:07.435
I doubt the United States would
voice any criticism.

00:05:07.435 --> 00:05:08.836
What about the constitution?!

00:05:08.836 --> 00:05:11.472
Do you plan on casting aside the
years of precedence and policy

00:05:11.472 --> 00:05:14.475
established on this issue
on your own accord?!

00:05:14.475 --> 00:05:18.605
As one who maintains the law, I
cannot agree to any such position!

00:05:19.981 --> 00:05:20.970
Prime Minister!

00:06:05.693 --> 00:06:08.963
Mr. Yushiro, we've come for you, Sir.

00:06:08.963 --> 00:06:11.732
Right, I need to talk to my
platoon commander.

00:06:11.732 --> 00:06:12.790
I'll be right back.

00:06:14.602 --> 00:06:20.598
If overseas deployment is finalized,
will Captain Gowa accompany us?

00:06:22.176 --> 00:06:24.041
I would imagine that
would be the case.

00:06:25.813 --> 00:06:28.316
I don't think we should
go ahead with this!

00:06:28.316 --> 00:06:32.587
Since Gowa was leading
the development effort,

00:06:32.587 --> 00:06:35.189
there may be good reason to have a
civilian such as Captain Gowa with us.

00:06:35.189 --> 00:06:38.092
But if we are going to be
deployed overseas,

00:06:38.092 --> 00:06:42.163
it is evident that this will be seen
as a combat operation

00:06:42.163 --> 00:06:45.066
no matter what we say to convince
them otherwise.

00:06:45.066 --> 00:06:49.867
Stating that this is part of the
development won't be enough.

00:06:52.807 --> 00:06:55.867
Gowa doesn't seem to think so.

00:06:57.111 --> 00:06:59.113
Gowa again?

00:06:59.113 --> 00:07:05.450
If we do see real combat, we may need
Captain Gowa's help more than ever.

00:07:10.291 --> 00:07:14.028
There's no question its capacities
are improving.

00:07:14.028 --> 00:07:16.963
But almost none of the most
fundamental problems are resolved.

00:07:18.199 --> 00:07:19.800
First is the question of why Mile One,

00:07:19.800 --> 00:07:24.805
or the adaptive artificial muscle
structure, only responds to Yushiro.

00:07:24.805 --> 00:07:28.342
And why changes to it are reflected
accurately by not only Yushiro's TA,

00:07:28.342 --> 00:07:31.402
but by all the other TA's as well.

00:07:32.880 --> 00:07:35.650
Are you at a total loss to explain it?

00:07:35.650 --> 00:07:39.020
There are just too many
variables involved.

00:07:39.020 --> 00:07:43.389
We've figured out that Mile One is a
huge collection of molecular motors,

00:07:44.659 --> 00:07:47.461
but we haven't figured
out anything else.

00:07:47.461 --> 00:07:51.666
A compound molecule comprised of
several billion atoms fused as one.

00:07:51.666 --> 00:07:54.936
That alone breaks all the rules of
physics, but on top of that,

00:07:54.936 --> 00:07:59.373
it seems an unimaginable amount of
information is stored within it.

00:07:59.373 --> 00:08:03.978
In that way, the giant molecule of
Mile One is like a DNA molecule.

00:08:03.978 --> 00:08:07.048
If we could find a complete structure,

00:08:07.048 --> 00:08:09.539
we would be able to speculate on
the shape of the original form.

00:08:10.751 --> 00:08:15.423
So, if there was no loss of
information in the sample,

00:08:15.423 --> 00:08:19.189
it might be possible to build an
entire kugai from scratch.

00:08:20.595 --> 00:08:23.264
Theoretically, that would be possible.

00:08:23.264 --> 00:08:27.969
But the sample we have at this time
has a lot of information missing,

00:08:27.969 --> 00:08:30.071
so something like that
would not be easy.

00:08:30.071 --> 00:08:31.939
What are the chances of success?

00:08:31.939 --> 00:08:36.143
Next to zero. The number of possible
combinations is infinite.

00:08:36.143 --> 00:08:39.814
Finding a complete structure
in something like that

00:08:39.814 --> 00:08:43.477
would be like finding a small
diamond in the desert.

00:08:45.586 --> 00:08:48.453
So that's the best we can
do for the moment.

00:08:51.959 --> 00:08:53.654
That's about the size of it.

00:08:56.030 --> 00:08:58.794
That's why we have Yushiro.

00:09:01.202 --> 00:09:02.803
Yushiro?

00:09:02.803 --> 00:09:06.440
We will supplement the missing parts

00:09:06.440 --> 00:09:08.101
by using him.

00:09:35.136 --> 00:09:37.204
It's a weather wheel.

00:09:37.204 --> 00:09:40.441
I never realized how low it was.

00:09:40.441 --> 00:09:43.944
It seems like it's been
a long, long time

00:09:43.944 --> 00:09:46.879
since father would pick me up so
I could spin the wheel.

00:09:51.619 --> 00:09:53.854
Why don't you spin it?

00:09:53.854 --> 00:09:54.843
Me?

00:09:56.490 --> 00:10:00.561
I understand that its for
predicting the weather,

00:10:00.561 --> 00:10:04.565
but big brother, you used to think the
spinning wheel might have the ability

00:10:04.565 --> 00:10:07.601
to grant the wishes of
those who spin it.

00:10:07.601 --> 00:10:11.799
Is there something you would
like to wish for, Misuzu?

00:10:13.908 --> 00:10:16.001
I have none.

00:10:17.778 --> 00:10:22.750
Yes, I have. But I cannot say it yet.

00:10:22.750 --> 00:10:24.240
If I should utter it,

00:10:25.586 --> 00:10:27.645
everything will fall apart.

00:10:30.357 --> 00:10:31.654
I cannot say it.

00:10:35.830 --> 00:10:38.799
Not yet. Not now.

00:10:38.799 --> 00:10:42.136
Only, please promise me

00:10:42.136 --> 00:10:43.704
that you will return.

00:10:43.704 --> 00:10:48.409
That you will return, dear brother,
no matter where you might go!

00:10:48.409 --> 00:10:50.311
You know.

00:10:50.311 --> 00:10:54.982
Why must this be?

00:10:54.982 --> 00:10:57.644
Even if you are... Even if you are...

00:11:09.163 --> 00:11:11.065
Don't worry.

00:11:11.065 --> 00:11:12.266
I'll be fine.

00:11:12.266 --> 00:11:15.903
Even if we are deployed, the primary
purpose is conducting trials.

00:11:15.903 --> 00:11:18.394
There's little chance
I'll see any action.

00:11:20.508 --> 00:11:22.676
I'm sorry.

00:11:22.676 --> 00:11:26.113
Oh, I'm apologizing again.

00:11:26.113 --> 00:11:27.944
I'm so peculiar.

00:11:39.890 --> 00:11:43.130
I've been told the overseas deployment
of the TA unit has been finalized.

00:11:43.130 --> 00:11:45.820
You'll most likely be departing
tomorrow morning.

00:11:51.900 --> 00:11:53.740
I understand.

00:11:53.740 --> 00:11:54.730
Wait.

00:11:55.810 --> 00:11:58.410
You don't have anything to say?

00:11:58.410 --> 00:12:00.340
No, nothing in particular.

00:12:06.880 --> 00:12:09.650
Sending Yushiro to Belgistan?

00:12:09.650 --> 00:12:12.490
Opportunities like this
don't come often.

00:12:12.490 --> 00:12:15.960
Even if we can recreate
a realistic situation,

00:12:15.960 --> 00:12:20.790
a simulation is still only a virtual
experience. Nothing like real combat.

00:12:22.370 --> 00:12:27.340
It's impossible to compare
it to battlefields

00:12:27.340 --> 00:12:29.570
where the real fear of death wanders
about everywhere.

00:12:29.570 --> 00:12:32.210
And there was the issue of the
explosion in Belgistan.

00:12:32.210 --> 00:12:35.380
We can't just ignore it.

00:12:35.380 --> 00:12:39.050
But how will the cabinet react?

00:12:39.050 --> 00:12:42.750
I'm told the Minister of Justice is
against deployment of the TA.

00:12:42.750 --> 00:12:44.620
Nothing out of the ordinary.

00:12:47.620 --> 00:12:50.230
Adamant about protecting the
constitution, I guess.

00:12:50.230 --> 00:12:53.420
The problem should be resolved soon.

00:12:56.430 --> 00:12:58.870
Five lost their lives in this accident,

00:12:58.870 --> 00:13:04.370
including the Minister of
Justice Kashiwada,

00:13:04.370 --> 00:13:06.240
who was on his way to a
speaking engagement.

00:13:06.240 --> 00:13:07.510
You knew about this?
who was on his way to a
speaking engagement.

00:13:07.510 --> 00:13:07.880
I see. It looks like America is
on the move as well.
who was on his way to a
speaking engagement.

00:13:07.880 --> 00:13:10.150
I see. It looks like America is
on the move as well.
The police are currently investigating
the accident scene.

00:13:10.150 --> 00:13:11.780
The police are currently investigating
the accident scene.

00:13:11.780 --> 00:13:14.440
We should have a live feed
from the scene soon.

00:13:15.690 --> 00:13:21.920
Is this information about America's
predawn invasion tomorrow reliable?

00:13:21.920 --> 00:13:26.020
We are certain that it will start within
the next nineteen hours.

00:13:27.030 --> 00:13:28.630
Please observe.

00:13:28.630 --> 00:13:34.170
This is a reconnaissance photo of
northern Kaha obtained from the US.

00:13:34.170 --> 00:13:35.570
Please look at these vehicles.

00:13:35.570 --> 00:13:39.580
US intelligence dismisses them
as being ordinary trucks,

00:13:39.580 --> 00:13:42.750
but according to Section One
Investigations Office,

00:13:42.750 --> 00:13:45.950
analysis reveals them to be transports
for their bipedal weapon.

00:13:45.950 --> 00:13:49.790
If the US Forces should fail in
their mission again,

00:13:49.790 --> 00:13:53.620
and if we could have our TA's come
in and defeat the enemy...

00:14:03.270 --> 00:14:05.700
Get me Kitajima in Geneva.

00:14:07.800 --> 00:14:11.940
For dispatching the TA's without
the Security Council's endorsement,

00:14:11.940 --> 00:14:13.240
I will take responsibility.

00:14:41.840 --> 00:14:44.710
Then what about retrieval of the
experimental facilities?

00:14:44.710 --> 00:14:48.740
We are simply waiting for Miharu's
condition to stabilize.

00:14:48.740 --> 00:14:51.010
The multinational forces are
gearing up rapidly.

00:14:51.010 --> 00:14:53.320
Hurry the work as much as you can.

00:14:53.320 --> 00:14:54.580
Understood, Sir.

00:14:54.580 --> 00:14:59.720
And regarding Stilbanov, he's
showing dangerous signs.

00:14:59.720 --> 00:15:03.490
It is all too clear that righteousness
prevails on our side!

00:15:03.490 --> 00:15:07.630
Regardless of this, the multinational
force, with America at its center,

00:15:07.630 --> 00:15:10.960
Damn puppet. It's going to his head.
continues its bombing of civilians!

00:15:21.780 --> 00:15:23.710
There's where the Aral Sea used to be.

00:15:23.710 --> 00:15:27.850
I read a vast inland sea
used to be there.

00:15:27.850 --> 00:15:32.120
But people came in droves, and
turned it into a desert.

00:15:36.690 --> 00:15:38.430
I'm sorry about this.

00:15:38.430 --> 00:15:40.760
Making you come along with us.

00:15:40.760 --> 00:15:43.000
Captain, you are still a civilian.

00:15:43.000 --> 00:15:45.670
But in the end, we...

00:15:45.670 --> 00:15:50.260
Even though we knew it was an unfair
order, we weren't able to oppose it.

00:15:54.580 --> 00:15:56.910
But I want you to trust us!

00:15:56.910 --> 00:16:01.220
We will make sure that you get
back to Japan unharmed.

00:16:01.220 --> 00:16:02.890
No matter what happens!

00:16:02.890 --> 00:16:04.650
Thank you very much.

00:16:04.650 --> 00:16:12.320
But I am participating in this operation
of my own free will.

00:16:27.180 --> 00:16:31.270
Charlie Bravo here. Alpha Company,
converge. We will now stand by.

00:16:54.040 --> 00:16:56.310
All companies reporting
preparations complete.

00:16:56.310 --> 00:16:57.140
Good.

00:16:59.010 --> 00:17:01.980
Thirty minutes until our assault.
Right on time.

00:17:10.990 --> 00:17:12.180
SP on!

00:17:16.560 --> 00:17:17.930
Sandstorm approaching, Sir!

00:17:17.930 --> 00:17:19.930
You should go below!

00:17:19.930 --> 00:17:21.400
Inform all units.

00:17:21.400 --> 00:17:22.970
I'll be fine.

00:17:22.970 --> 00:17:24.100
You go below.

00:17:24.100 --> 00:17:28.600
Line to Gun, SB will only last thirty
seconds. Forwarding radar image.

00:17:28.600 --> 00:17:29.570
M1!

00:17:29.570 --> 00:17:32.200
Execute operation as specified
in the pre-briefing.

00:17:35.210 --> 00:17:36.410
M2!

00:17:41.020 --> 00:17:42.890
What is it? Report!

00:17:42.890 --> 00:17:44.920
ATM! We've been ambushed!

00:17:44.920 --> 00:17:47.560
A surprise attack?
Locate enemy position!

00:17:47.560 --> 00:17:49.060
Emergency evasive action!

00:17:49.060 --> 00:17:50.720
All units, fire at will.
Hit them where it hurts!

00:17:52.930 --> 00:17:56.270
Heat source at 3 o'clock! Targeting.

00:17:56.270 --> 00:17:58.400
Do it! Lay down cover fire!

00:17:58.400 --> 00:17:59.670
Fire away without precise aiming!

00:17:59.670 --> 00:18:00.730
Fire away!

00:18:13.880 --> 00:18:16.550
Time to move out! All units prepare
for close range engagement.

00:18:16.550 --> 00:18:19.020
Alpha Eight here!
Enemy is coming out.

00:18:19.020 --> 00:18:23.330
Targets: two, correction, four at our
10 o'clock, and four at our 1 o'clock!

00:18:23.330 --> 00:18:24.860
Cannot identify enemy!

00:18:24.860 --> 00:18:26.560
Alpha Company, to the left flank!

00:18:26.560 --> 00:18:29.130
Beta Company, position yourself
to Alpha Company's left flank!

00:18:29.130 --> 00:18:30.500
Formation A!

00:18:30.500 --> 00:18:32.230
Roger! Vehicle forward!

00:18:32.230 --> 00:18:33.540
Balls to the wall!

00:18:33.540 --> 00:18:34.940
Yes, Sir. Forward!

00:18:34.940 --> 00:18:36.430
Run!

00:18:37.770 --> 00:18:38.870
M3!

00:18:55.460 --> 00:18:57.260
Major, fall back and watch our rear.

00:18:57.260 --> 00:18:59.500
Colonel, you must fall back as well!

00:18:59.500 --> 00:19:00.430
This is a direct order.

00:19:00.430 --> 00:19:01.920
Yes, Sir!
This is a direct order.

00:19:08.170 --> 00:19:10.310
Enemy continues to advance.

00:19:10.310 --> 00:19:12.970
Maximum combat speed.
All units forward!

00:19:15.180 --> 00:19:17.780
Visual! Enemy identified
as heavy infantrymen!

00:19:17.780 --> 00:19:19.080
Men, prepare to move out!

00:19:19.080 --> 00:19:20.980
What?! That's too big!

00:19:20.980 --> 00:19:23.610
Hold it! Cancel that last order!

00:19:25.190 --> 00:19:27.120
G-30! AP round!

00:19:27.120 --> 00:19:30.160
Lieutenant, what the devil is that?!

00:19:30.160 --> 00:19:32.700
I don't care! Combat targeting!

00:19:32.700 --> 00:19:33.760
Three round bursts!

00:19:33.760 --> 00:19:36.630
Target... Who the hell cares?! Fire!

00:19:39.100 --> 00:19:40.590
Spin!

00:19:43.010 --> 00:19:43.990
Smoke!

00:19:50.280 --> 00:19:51.210
He's on top of us!

00:19:51.210 --> 00:19:51.780
Traverse turret! Shake him off!
He's on top of us!

00:19:51.780 --> 00:19:53.270
Traverse turret! Shake him off!

00:19:57.920 --> 00:19:59.990
Damn it, it's too close!

00:19:59.990 --> 00:20:02.020
Warn all tanks not to
fire at one another!

00:20:02.020 --> 00:20:06.200
IFV's switch to five round bursts of
HE rounds, and lay down cover fire!

00:20:06.200 --> 00:20:08.530
Do not let your infantry out unless
under exceptional circumstances!

00:20:24.150 --> 00:20:27.120
I can't keep up! The turret won't
move fast enough!

00:20:27.120 --> 00:20:30.590
Damn it, Alpha Eight to all Alpha units!

00:20:30.590 --> 00:20:33.850
Restrain free use of MBT main
gun, all units fall back!

00:20:40.960 --> 00:20:43.330
Bastard, I'll run you over!

00:20:50.040 --> 00:20:51.240
Keep going! Keep going!

00:20:51.240 --> 00:20:52.470
Run him over!

00:20:54.110 --> 00:20:55.470
Eat this, you son of a bitch!

00:20:57.910 --> 00:20:59.400
M4!

00:21:00.620 --> 00:21:01.550
Evacuate!

00:21:08.090 --> 00:21:09.060
Count up!

00:21:09.060 --> 00:21:09.590
Mission clear. All missions completed.
Count up!

00:21:09.590 --> 00:21:11.830
Mission clear. All missions completed.

00:21:11.830 --> 00:21:13.500
Everyone, you did a good job.

00:21:13.500 --> 00:21:15.220
All units, return to base!

00:21:19.770 --> 00:21:21.600
Cease firing!

00:21:21.600 --> 00:21:23.370
Beta Three, we've lost
combat capacity.

00:21:23.370 --> 00:21:25.710
Alpha 21, treads disabled.

00:21:25.710 --> 00:21:29.780
Beta IFV 14, turret has suffered
moderate damage, unable to move.

00:21:29.780 --> 00:21:33.520
Alpha Company, Commander
Captain Smith, KIA.

00:21:33.520 --> 00:21:36.810
We're breaking radio silence.
Get me regimental HQ.

00:21:38.320 --> 00:21:41.060
Sir, regimental HQ!

00:21:41.060 --> 00:21:42.060
Colonel!

00:21:42.060 --> 00:21:44.360
Higgins here. Regimental
headquarters?

00:21:44.360 --> 00:21:49.700
My battalion was hit by an enemy
ambush, and sustained heavy losses.

00:21:49.700 --> 00:21:52.500
We can no longer proceed with
Operation Desert Fox.

00:21:54.140 --> 00:21:56.230
I'm sorry, Regiment Commander.

00:21:57.810 --> 00:22:01.740
How could they have predicted
our movements?!

00:22:01.740 --> 00:22:07.220
It appears that Belgistan has some
powerful backing we were unaware of.

00:22:07.220 --> 00:22:09.220
We'll discuss this later.

00:22:09.220 --> 00:22:11.090
Backing?

00:22:11.090 --> 00:22:14.390
A transnational corporate
conglomerate

00:22:14.390 --> 00:22:17.760
with intelligence capabilities
that match ours.

00:22:17.760 --> 00:22:24.320
Someway, they must be supplying
Belgistan with their bipedal weapons.

00:22:25.770 --> 00:22:28.360
Bipedal weapons?

00:22:28.400 --> 00:22:33.220
Hark

00:22:34.380 --> 00:22:39.670
It's time I journey

00:22:43.200 --> 00:22:50.340
Break apart my heart

00:22:50.510 --> 00:22:56.870
For crimson sadness

00:22:57.200 --> 00:23:04.380
Pours out from it

00:23:04.590 --> 00:23:08.300
I can only, oh

00:23:08.410 --> 00:23:11.490
Close my eyes, oh

00:23:11.580 --> 00:23:17.100
I pray, let this break apart

00:23:32.320 --> 00:23:36.200
I can only, oh

00:23:36.290 --> 00:23:39.350
Close my eyes, oh

00:23:39.420 --> 00:23:44.550
I pray, let this break apart

00:23:46.080 --> 00:23:52.530
I beg you, be by my side

00:23:59.500 --> 00:24:01.460
The guns have stopped.

00:24:01.460 --> 00:24:04.830
Winds blow through this barren land.

00:24:04.830 --> 00:24:07.600
Suddenly my body is held captive.

00:24:07.600 --> 00:24:11.440
My hands, my legs, my consciousness,

00:24:11.440 --> 00:24:14.010
all guided by forces I cannot resist,

00:24:14.010 --> 00:24:16.210
are made to dance the Gasara.

00:24:16.210 --> 00:24:17.780
Hollowness of time

00:24:17.780 --> 00:24:20.120
Flowing about, but in its chasm
something beckons

00:24:20.120 --> 00:24:24.050
I see the mirage that manipulates
me all too well.

00:24:24.050 --> 00:24:27.540
There is someone inside
me I do not know.
